  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 243 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nNocturnal and morning convection, mainly across northern Iowa, is \nexpected to continue each day through at least Sunday morning. With \nonly modest forcing severe chances each day are fairly low. The next \nmore organized convection chance is not until early next week and \nthat will help to squash the ridge and bring at least some relief to \ntemperatures for a few days. Until then, heat continues this weekend \nwith heat indicies in the upper 90s to low 100s across southern and \ninto central Iowa. With the holiday weekend coming up it is \nimportant to remember heat safety for any outdoor plans that are in \nplace. Minimize time outside, hydrate, and take breaks in the shade. \nBy late week the thermal ridge looks to rebuild with heat and \nhumidity lifting back north into the area, along with continued \nscattered storm chances.",
